knowledge {
  anthem {
    Anthem's Underlying Provider Directory FHIR APIAnthem serves its public Provider Directory API via Elevance Health's totalview.healthos.elevancehealth.com gateway (documented at [anthem.com/developers](https://anthem.com/developers) and [totalview.healthos.elevancehealth.com/fhir/documentation](https://totalview.healthos.elevancehealth.com/fhir/documentation)):Base Endpoint Pattern: [https://totalview.healthos.elevancehealth.com/resources/registered/](https://totalview.healthos.elevancehealth.com/resources/registered/){Brand}/api/v1/fhir (where {Brand} corresponds to the regional/plan brand such as AnthemBlueCross or Anthem)Authentication: None required for the public Provider Directory endpoints (unlike the Patient Access API, which requires SMART on FHIR / OAuth 2.0).   Supported FHIR Resources for Doctor Search:Practitioner — Search by name, family, given, or identifier (NPI).   PractitionerRole — Links a doctor to their specialty, location, organization, and network.   Location — Search by address, city, state, or postal code.   Organization & InsurancePlan — Filter by hospital/clinic group and specific Anthem plan network.
  }
}

question_llm: ornith-1.5:35b

anthem_plan_member_id: {directory_of_this_prompt}/.chat/anthem/member_id.txt

group unit_tests {
  task (completed) {
    1. type /anthem
    2. tell me about Johannes Kratz, MD in UCSF
    3. it should show the doctor's detail
    apply to all doctors
  }

  task (completed) {
    in the result list, we should only have "In Network" and "Out Of Network", we should not have "Network Unknown (Member Plan)"
  }

  task (completed) {
    in the result list, each entry has:
    Network Unknown (Member Plan) · Network Unknown (Anthem PPO) · Network Unknown (Anthem BlueCard National PPO)

    - we do not need to look up Anthem PPO and Anthem BlueCard National PPO, we just need to look for Member Plan, we need to say if the doctor or facility is In Network or Out Of Network
  }

  task (completed) {
    questoin: show me a list of head and neck cancer doctors in md anderson
    expect: Shirley Y. Su, MBBS, FRACS should be in the list
    actual: this doctor is not in the list
  }

  task (completed) {
    can you double check if Karen Y. Choi, MD, FACS in Anthem Blue Cross BlueChoice National PPO or not
  }

  task (completed) {
    can you double check if UT MD Anderson Cancer Center is in Anthem Blue Cross BlueChoice National PPO or not
  }

  task (completed) {
    the In Network or Out of Network information should show in the list of results
  }

  task (completed) {
    when i click on Johannes Kratz, MD:
    expect: in "Education & Training" and "Awards & Recognition", it should have good information
    actural: Not found in the retrieved public records
    please fix it in a systematic way, find ways to gather these information for any doctor
  }

  task (completed) {
    refer to task.ucsf_only_doctors:
    question: find list of lung cancer specialists only in ucsf
    expect: the result should contain Johannes Kratz, MD
    actual: Johannes Kratz, MD is not in the list
    please fix in a systematic way
  }

  task (completed) {
    refer to task.ucsf_only_doctors:
    question: find list of head and neck cancer specialists only in ucsf
    expect: the result should contain a list of doctors in UCSF only
    actual: Patrick Carpenter MD is in the list
  }

  task.ucsf_only_doctors (completed) {
    after typing the command /anthem {
      question: find list of head and neck cancer specialists only in ucsf
      expect: the result should contain a list of doctors in UCSF only
      actual: SAI DEEPIKA CHALLAPALLI, MD is in the result, this doctor is in 450 SUTTER ST and is not in UCSF
      please fix this issue in a systematic way
    }
  }

  task (completed) {
    question: pediatric otolaryngology in UCSF
    expect: the provider's name (such as doctor's name) should appear
    actual: doctor's name is not presented
  }
}

group application {
  task.feature.free_form_question (completed) {
    question: i want to have a surgery on my lung tumor, give me some doctors who are specialized in this field in ucsf
    expect: it should show me a list of doctors with surgery and lung cancer experience, including Johannes Kratz, MD
    please implement it in a systematic way
  }

  task.bug.show_n_doctors_in_hospital (completed) {
    - question: show me all lung cancer doctors in UCSF
    - what happened: Johannes Kratz, MD is not in the list
    please fix it in a systematic way
  }

  task.feature.show_n_doctors_in_hospital (completed) {
    - question: show me N head and neck doctors in UCSF
    - answer: we should see only list of at most N doctors in UCSF
    apply to all "show me N doctors in specialty in a facility" type of question
  }

  task.anthem_as_an_online_tool (completed) {
    - make /anthem a tool that the chat can invoke when chat mode is "Online"
    - for example:
    question: tell me about Shirley Su, MD in MD Anderson
    answer should contain this doctor's detail
  }

  task.feature.direct_doctor_detail (completed) {
    question: tell me about Johannes Kratz, MD in UCSF
    answer: it should show me the doctor's detail
  }

  task.optimization.speed_up_result_list (completed) {
    the list of doctors still take a long time to load, please speed it up
  }

  task.feature.speed_up_result_list (completed) {
    1. Send the provider list immediately and annotate network status asynchronously, either via later SSE updates or a separate endpoint. This alone
    would reduce perceived load from ~66s to ~3s.
    2. Use the NPI-based lookup/v1/provider call first, instead of trying all search-box prefixes first.
    3. Deduplicate PPO/BlueCard/member-plan lookups since the same provider lookup is repeated across plan groups.
    4. Annotate on demand when a card is opened, or only annotate the first page of results.
    5. Persist the status cache by NPI + state + plan prefix so restarts do not lose it.
    6. Use the registered Anthem FHIR Directory if credentials become available, since _anthem_network() already reads network participation from PractitionerRole and would avoid the Find Care calls entirely.
  }

  task.feature.result_summary_plus_detail (completed) {
    when openning the provider's detail modal, the result summary is overwritten by the detail:
    for example, the detail modal should constain something like :
    Internal Medicine, Critical Care Medicine license Q4798 (TX); Internal Medicine, Pulmonary Disease (primary) license Q4798 (TX) · 1515 HOLCOMBE BLVD, HOUSTON, TX 770304000 · 713-792-6161 · In Network (Member Plan) · In Network (Anthem PPO) · In Network (Anthem BlueCard National PPO)
    <the doctor's detail>
  }

  task.feature.member_id_reverse_plan_search (completed) {
    the anthem plan member id is located at the file {anthem_plan_member_id}
    based on the anthem plan id, tell me if the doctors or facilities are in network or not
  }

  task.feature.anthem_bluecross_bluecard_national_ppo (completed) {
    please show me if the doctors or hospital/facilities are in network in anthem bluecross bluecard national ppo or not
  }

  task.feature.in_network_confirmation (completed) {
    for each doctor or provider in the result list, please add a flag to mention if the provider is in Anthem PPO Plan
  }

  task.feature.follow_up_question_on_doctor (completed) {
    - type: /anthem
    - type "find list of lung cancer specialists only in ucsf"
    - now, type: tell me more about Johannes Kratz, MD
    - requirement:
    it should return me the detail of Johannes Kratz, MD
    the context should be aware of the list of doctors in UCSF
  }

  task.feature.specialist_title (completed) {
    in the list of results, if the entry is a specalist, add the specialist's academic title, for example:
    - YEW SONG CHENG, MD's Academic title is "Clinical Professor"
  }

  task.feature.show_providers_result_instantly (completed) {
    - currrently, when presenting list of results, it uses {question_llm} to generate the list
    DO NOT do that, instead, just use related apis or mcps to give me the result ASAP
  }

  task.feature.provider_detail_modal (completed) {
    each one of the provider's result should be an url, when clicked {
      - open up a modal, similar to the /article command's article loader
      - the modal should {
        - show the provider's detail, for example if it's a doctor, show his or her background introduction, research interest, education background, awards...etc
      }
    }
  }

  task.initial_spec (completed) {

    create command: /anthem <question> {
      logic.question(<question>) {
        - a specific doctor's name
        - a specific doctor's name in a specific medical facility (hospital, clinics, lab.. etc)
        - a list of doctors in a specific specialty (head and neck, lung, heart...)
        - a list of doctors in a specific hospital, medical university (UCSF, Standford, MD Anderson... etc)

        requirement:
        - it should use {question_llm}
        - it should allow follow up questions and maintain question to question context similar to the main chat
      }
      - if <question> is presented, it should allow me to search:
      perform logic.question(<question>)
      - if <question> is not presented:
      - clear all existing accumulated context in the chat
      - perform logic.question(<question>)
    }
  }
}
